# Lab 1 – Matrix Multiplication using Sequential C and OpenMP

## Objective

To implement matrix multiplication using sequential programming and OpenMP parallel programming, and compare their execution performance.

## Description

In this lab, matrix multiplication is performed on two square matrices of size 4000 × 4000.

The sequential version performs the matrix multiplication using a normal nested-loop approach.

The OpenMP version uses parallel processing to distribute the matrix multiplication work among multiple CPU threads.

The execution time and correctness of the matrix multiplication are verified.

## Matrix Size

- Matrix A: 4000 × 4000
- Matrix B: 4000 × 4000
- Result Matrix C: 4000 × 4000

